 ticket_id resolution in _engine_support/gates.py for check-ac/clarity-check) and specify the emit insertion point for each, rather than treating require_id as the single shared gate.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.1,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Registry: `show`/`deps`/`ready`/`next-batch` route to handler `rebar._engine_support.reads:main` (_registry.py:179,183); `check-ac`/`clarity-check` route to `rebar._engine_support.gates:check_ac_cli`/`clarity_check_cli` (_registry.py:249,257)","`search_files require_id` in `src/rebar/_engine_support/` returns (no matches) — the read/gate arms never call require_id","reads.py:345,504 resolve via `resolve_ticket_id(ticket_id, tracker)`; gates.py:93 sets `ticket_id = ns.ticket_id ...` then calls `check_ac_compute` directly","Plan Scope names only `src/rebar/_cli/` and `_seam.py`(require_id); it says 'the id resolution the read arms use' but does not name resolve_ticket_id / reads.py / gates.py"],"finding":"The plan asserts `require_id` is 'the shared resolution seam used by both single-ticket and non-single-ticket paths' and 'the single gate', but read commands `show`/`deps` and gate commands `check-ac`/`clarity-check` in the allowlist do NOT flow through `require_id`. `show`/`deps` resolve ids via `resolve_ticket_id` inside `rebar._engine_support/reads.py:main` (see reads.py:345,504), and `check-ac`/`clarity-check` resolve their own `ticket_id` inside `rebar._engine_support/gates.py` (check_ac_cli, gates.py:81-94) and call `check_ac_compute`, never touching `require_id`. Instrumenting only `require_id` (+ '_cli/') would leave the `show`/`deps`/`check-ac`/`clarity-check` allowlist entries un-warned, and the plan's Scope does not enumerate `_engine_support/reads.py` or `_engine_support/gates.py` as edit targets.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb56e295cc9ba369f","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach ('the shared resolution seam') + Scope ('src/rebar/_cl